Futya
======

Futya is a Low-Level and a Efficient Operating System for ARM64 Arch, written in Assembly, C, C++, Java and JavaScript.

Quick Start
------------
Find your first start:
  * LLM or AI Assistant: See Documentation/AI-LLM/coding-assistant.
  * Core Assembly Developer: See Arch/
  * Kernel Developer: See Arch/Kernel/
  * Learning code bare-metal: Shut up, show me code.
  * See SubModules: qemu/, googletest/ or .gitmodules.
  * GOVERNANCE: See GOVERNANCE.
  * License: See LICENSE.
  * ROADMAP and Changelog: See ROADMAP.rst and CHANGELOG.rst.
  * Contributing: See CONTRIBUTING
  * Build: See .azurepipelines/, .devcontainer/ or .github/.
  * Docker: See .devcontainer/ or .dockerignore.
  * View Maintainers: See MAINTAINERS.
  * Git: See .gitattributes, .gitignore or .gitmodules.
  * Editor: See .editorconfig

Who Are You?
-------------
Find your role below:
  * Core Assembly Developer,
  * LLM or AI,
  * Human helped per AI/LLM,
  * Learning bare-metal code,
  * See Git Roles,
  * See Build Compilation,
  * and others.

